-- Heroic dungeon DamageModifier, step 1: elites/bosses of expansion 0-2 content (TBC/WotLK heroics, old-world dungeons in heroic form)
-- in creature_template_difficulty DUNGEON_HEROIC (695 rows), recalibrated the same way as fix 29 did for DUNGEON_NORMAL.
-- Cause: the heroic rows still carry the SkyFire-era dmg_multiplier of the heroic template (median 9-14, up to 125) on top of the
-- full per-level base table, so heroic elites hit 3-10x harder than the reference and 5x harder than the (fix29 calibrated) normal
-- version of the same creature (heroic/normal per-hit ratio before: p10 0.9, median 5, p90 11.9; reference: 1.3-1.7).
-- Method (identical to fix 29): new DM = ref_cpp heroic DM x ref_cpp base(level, class, exp) / our base(level, class, exp) =
--   same damage per second as the Cataclysm Preservation heroic template, reproduced on our base table. Heroic entries are
--   resolved through ref_cpp.creature_template.difficulty_entry_1 of the normal entry; clamp 0.5 .. 30; rows within 15% are skipped.
--   R2: ref_cpp heroic DM is the 1.0 placeholder (14 elites, e.g. Black Knight): live normal DM x 1.28 (lowest ref_cpp heroic/normal
--       ratio of the elite cohort; quantiles 1.28 / 1.73) re-based to the heroic level.
--   R6 floor: a heroic elite/boss never hits less than 1.28 x its live normal version (same instance +-3 levels).
--   R5: one cap at 30 where no reference exists.
--   Rank 0 (trash/adds) with a heroic DM <= 3 is left alone. Level-1 placeholder rows (level_min = 1) are left alone. Normal rows are not touched.
-- Source: ref_cpp (Cataclysm Preservation TDB434.22011 sniffs) creature_template + creature_classlevelstats, our creature_classlevelstats;
--         formula Creature::UpdateDamagePhysical (StatSystem.cpp, per hit = base x attack time x DM for expansion < 4).
--         Check: Ingvar the Plunderer (23954) heroic 18,670 -> 4,393 min swing (normal after fix 29: ~2,450); Kael'thas (24664) heroic 5,467 -> 1,242.
-- Rollback: every UPDATE carries the old value in its trailing comment; the complete script is
--           state/hdm/heroic_dm_rollback_10.sql (UPDATE ... SET DamageModifier = <old> WHERE id = <id> AND difficulty = 'DUNGEON_HEROIC').
-- Repeatable: plain UPDATEs keyed on (id, difficulty); no INSERTs, level_min/level_max untouched.


